  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7e763e05-fe76-53ec-a393-d068fd77c766" activityNameId="d529b21e-1c48-58da-871a-3eccca51390a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ventilator unit 1800 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ventilator unit 1800 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer, at plant
Production of a ventilator unit for a air handling unit with 1800 m3/h nominal air flow rate (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger). Reference value of inventory is 1 m3/h air flow. Specific component weight: 0.1 kg/(m3/h), total weight: 0.15 kg/(m3/h), including average components for controls, inverter and electric control cabinet, material for 20 filter replacements (once a year for 20 years lifetime). The ventilator of the air handling unit includes a frame construction, one radial belt drive fan, multi-leaf damper. No heat recovery, heating and/or cooling elements, humidifier, air-mixing plenum and silencer included. The frame construction made of aluminium-profiles, casing made of hot-dip galvanized and powder coated steel sheets insulated with polyurethane foam.
Materials used for the production. Energy use for the different production steps and for heating the production building. Transport of raw materials to the plant. Estimation for infrastructure of the production site included.
Location:  Data sources mainly from Switzerland. Process applicable in central European conditions.
Technology: Typical technology, materials and components used for ventilation systems in commercial and public buildings
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Process information from 2003 to 2012
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Manufacturer informations and literature data. Data of typical product used.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d04a86f8-03c1-3d8a-abb1-c3441eaef207.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
